ui-the-container-holds-multiple-tabs-which-can-be-fixed-or-scrollable-it-spans-the-full-width = The container holds multiple tabs, which can be fixed or scrollable. It spans the full width of the window and is divided into equal sections, one for each tab. A divider runs along its bottom edge, and the content below may scroll under it.

ui-the-container-is-the-area-that-contains-the-tabs-directly-under-the-title-above = The container is the area that contains the tabs directly under the title above

ui-icons-should-be-simple-and-recognizable-and-clearly-communicate-the-kind-of-content-a-tab = Icons should be simple and recognizable, and clearly communicate the kind of content a tab holds. Icons alone are less effective than labels, so use them with caution.

